// claim: `##.x` Float, `###x` Int (round),
// claim: `##!x` Int (truncate). A character and its code cross through `0d|…|` only: `0d|'A'|` is `65`,
// claim: `0d|65|` is `'A'`, and a code with no character is an error; `0x|c|`, `0o|c|`, `0b|c|` write
// claim: its code as text (`"0x41"`), and `0x|"41"|` reads it back.
x = 2.7
n = 65
>> ###x ¶             // → 3
>> ##!x ¶             // → 2
>> ##.n + 0.5 ¶       // → 65.5
>> 0d|n| ¶            // → A
>> 0d|'A'| ¶          // → 65
>> 0x|'A'| ¶          // → 0x41
>> 0x|"41"| ¶         // → A
